{
 "note": "R49 \u2014 PS4 EA-Opus (SNS codec 0x0c, NHL 18\u201321) sample-preview decode contract with known vectors. Read-only on the banks; the only writes\nare temporary Ogg / WAV files in the session scratchpad (removed unless --keep).\n\nChain measured per sample: `.sbr` DSET record (.SID, .OFF, .DUR) \u2192 `.sbs` SNS block stream (0x48 header = SNR: codec 0x0c, 48 000 Hz, channel\nconfig, num_samples; 0x44 data blocks: u24 size | u32 samples-in-block | payload; 0x45 end) \u2192 payload = u16 BE length-prefixed Opus packets\ntiling the payload exactly \u2192 each packet's TOC byte (RFC 6716 \u00a73.1: config \u2192 mode / bandwidth / frame duration; stereo bit; frame-count code)\n\u2192 frame count \u00d7 duration summed over the packets = the Opus sample count (48 kHz) \u2192 compared with the SNR num_samples, the data blocks'\nsamples-in-block and the DSET .DUR. Then the packets are re-framed as an Ogg Opus stream (OpusHead, OpusTags, one page per packet, granule =\ncumulative 48 kHz samples + pre-skip) and decoded with the locally installed ffmpeg (libopus / opus) to WAV; the decoded sample count is\ncompared with the declared count. Decode only \u2014 no encoder is claimed. Vectors: N records from each title's `pbp_samples_inxp.sbr` (or the\nlargest bank), chosen deterministically (first, last and evenly spaced .SIDs), with SHA-256 of the raw SNS bytes and of the decoded PCM.\nUsage: python r49_ea_opus_preview_vectors.py <out.json> [--titles nhl18,nhl19,nhl20,nhl21] [--per-title 6] [--keep]\n",
